       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the maximum for extended-release is 2,000 mg/day. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day in divided doses**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** at a different frequency\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
